A synchronous FIFO uses a single clock for both write and read operations. It is structurally simple: a dual-port memory with write and read pointers.

### Architecture

```
            +-----------+
  wr_data ->| Dual-port |-> rd_data
  wr_en   ->|  Memory   |<- rd_en
            +-----------+
               ^     ^
               |     |
            wr_ptr  rd_ptr
               |     |
            +--+-----+--+
            | Count/Flag |
            |   Logic    |
            +------------+
            full  empty  count
```

